  "visualBrief": "Present cream-black-cream tapering painted-brick lighthouse, sparse deeply recessed sash lights, flared pale neck and ten-sided projecting corbelled gallery, open pale/gold iron rail, tall gridded decagonal lantern with guard hoops, shallow pyramidal roof/ventilator. Native reconstructed two-storey keeper house with red standing-seam hip roof, small dormer, white chimney, bracketed cornice, five upper front sashes/two round lower lights, central entrance/stairs and open paired-column wraparound porch/balustrade, lower rear rooms and low tower link. Detached oil house/former assistant quarters, gardens and nearby buildings excluded.",
